{"id": "sdqa0123", "pool": "sdqa", "arm": "balanced", "tier": "balanced", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 2349223084, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "f4bb2b6e6cb68bd1527d1ee0e21321345a1bb395842da8101a511dc9dc7ef77e", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.7972545623779297, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 3, "query": "When did the British Empire end?", "input_path": "/data/sdqa_audio/sdqa0123.wav", "input_sha256": "8e235060d23aeab3018c6e6f3a48821e01a75ec96945dde8d1b991cc863c6dde", "input_samples": 47098, "input_s": 2.944, "n_real_chunks": 3, "score": 0.3504, "act": 0.9992, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "The British Empire didn' t end all at once. It slowly faded over many years. Most of its territories gained independence in the mid-1 9 50s and early 1 96 0s, especially after World War II when there was a lot of pressure for self-rule. India became independent in 1 947, Pakistan in 194 7, and then other countries like Nigeria in 19 60 and Ghana earlier than that. By the late 1 9 60s, most places had left the empire. So you could say it officially ended around that time, but it was a long process.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 37, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/sdqa/audio/sdqa0123_balanced_local.wav", "sha256": "3bc4d7a6544d69d38f54ce173b18fb9319e684c3dbfc5e6e4db72a9170403837", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 37.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.084, 1.152, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.074, 2.133, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 2.944, 3.019, 3.079, 1, 0, 0], [3, 0, 3.944, 4.016, 4.724, 0, 24000, 0], [4, 0, 4.944, 5.02, 